          <declname>SupportConcurrentCompilation</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>If set, this forces <ref refid="classllvm_1_1orc_1_1_l_l_j_i_t" kindref="compound">LLJIT</ref> concurrent compilation support to be either on or off. </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>This controls the selection of compile function (concurrent vs single threaded) and whether or not sub-modules are cloned to new contexts for lazy emission.</para>
<para>If not explicitly set then concurrency support will be turned on if NumCompileThreads is set to a non-zero value, or if a custom <ref refid="classllvm_1_1orc_1_1_execution_session" kindref="compound">ExecutionSession</ref> or <ref refid="classllvm_1_1orc_1_1_executor_process_control" kindref="compound">ExecutorProcessControl</ref> instance is provided. </para>
